 "brief": "GAUSSIAN FLUCTUATIONS OF JACK-DEFORMED RANDOM YOUNG DIAGRAMS — We introduce a large class of random Young diagrams which can be regarded as a natural one-parameter deformation of some classi- cal",
 "extended": "**GAUSSIAN FLUCTUATIONS OF JACK-DEFORMED RANDOM YOUNG DIAGRAMS**\n\n*MACIEJ DOŁ ˛EGA AND PIOTR ŚNIADY*\n\n43 pp, 47 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We introduce a large class of random Young diagrams which can be regarded as a natural one-parameter deformation of some classi- cal Young diagram ensembles; a deformation which is related to Jack polynomials and Jack characters. We show that each such a random Young diagram converges asymptotically to some limit shape and that the ﬂuctuations around the limit are asymptotically Gaussian.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Random partitions…; 1.2 …and random matrices; 1.3 Random Young diagrams related to log-gases; 1.4 Random Young diagrams and characters; 1.5 Irreducible characters of symmetric groups; 1.6 Irreducible Jack characters; 1.7 Probability measures P(); 1.8 Random Young diagrams related to Thoma's c; 1.9 Cumulants; 1.10 Asymptotics; 1.11 Hypothesis: asymptotics of; 1.12 Hypothesis: approximate factorization of ; 1.13 Drawing Young diagrams; 1.14 The first main result: Law of Large Numbe; 1.15 The second main result: Central Limit The; 1.16 Example",
